# Force LF line endings for text files, regardless of each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, Windows checkouts silently convert
# LF -> CRLF, which breaks any content-hash check (sha256, etc) computed
# against the file on disk: the git blob (what CI on Linux checks out) has
# LF, so a hash captured on a Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true
# stops matching on Ubuntu runners. Root-caused 2026-09-30 in M0.3a CI:
# knowledge/registries/{agents,prompts}/registry.storage.json stored
# CRLF-derived sha256 values for all 11 of their entries; all 11 failed on
# ubuntu-latest while passing on windows-latest. See
# governance/roadmaps/AI-NATIVE-V3-ROADMAP.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep their native line endings.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
